id: pmc-wvnz
title: Raise pm-changelog source coverage gates to 100/100/100
description: "The real TypeScript coverage gate is present and prevents file omission, but its enforced floor remains 89/78/90. The current authoritative run passes 212 tests at 90.36% lines, 80.08% branches, and 90.91% functions, which does not satisfy the ecosystem's mandatory 100/100/100 requirement."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: code-quality,coverage,release-blocker,testing
created_at: "2026-08-01T23:22:30.309Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T21:20:39.942Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T21:06:26.343Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T21:06:26.343Z"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "Every executable source line branch and function is exercised by meaningful unit integration and black-box tests; package coverage thresholds are exactly 100/100/100 and cannot be reduced without a failing policy test; the source-file inventory negative control remains; tests do not use ignore pragmas artificial calls or implementation-free mocks to inflate coverage; real CLI SDK package-install and GitHub workflow behavior remains covered; npm run release:check reports exact 100 percent for every dimension"
reviewer: steve
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: coverage-hardening
release: 2026.8.5
severity: high
resolution: "The child pmc-p5l1 completed the remaining CLI, extension, and generator coverage; PR #127 merged the exact 100/100/100 thresholds and all-source presence control."
expected_result: "The authoritative release gate enforces and reaches exact 100 percent line, branch, and function coverage across every production source."
actual_result: "Delivered by child pmc-p5l1: merged PR #127 raised the fail-closed inventory gate to exact 100.00% lines, 100.00% branches, and 100.00% functions for all nine measured production sources. The post-review 2026-08-20 release gate reports the same exact coverage with 389 passing tests."
component: test/coverage-gate
customer_impact: "The original uncovered-path regression risk is resolved for every measured production source by the exact 100/100/100 all-source gate. The remaining ecosystem mandate gap is narrower and separately tracked in pmc-ilrh: the Node/V8 report does not expose an independently justified statement percentage."
